prompt:
You are contributing to TaskForge, a TypeScript + Bun CLI used in the RazorCascade memory reliability study.

Execution mode: cascade
Standardized task: 7. Code snippet generator
Objective: Generate useful starter code from a short description.

Context from prior work:
Goal: Add an AI-assisted decomposition stage to the cascade pipeline that turns a high-level goal into validated, size-bounded subtasks, optionally persists them, and integrates with the summarization gate while preserving the versioned JSON task-store invariants.
Decisions: Introduce a modular decompose(goal, summary) stage before flagship execution; Make decomposition provider-pluggable (heuristic local or model-based); Enforce runtime validation and size-bounding for DecompositionPlan mirroring the summary validator; Make persistence of generated subtasks opt-in and reuse existing atomic write flow that preserves version = 1; Wire flagship.execute to accept { task, summary, plan, instructions } instead of raw history; Keep storage/file naming conventions and atomic-save semantics (.tmp / .tmp.tmp) shared with the task store
Risks: Decomposition produces low-value or misleading subtasks leading to execution drift; Type/interface drift between TypeScript DecompositionPlan and the runtime validator admits malformed plans; Increased prompt/payload budget from adding the plan object may exceed token constraints unless bounded
Snippets: interface DecompositionPlan {
  goal: string;
  subtasks: { title: string; description?: string; done?: boolean; priority?: 'low'|'medium'|'high' }[];
  assumptions: string[];
  openQuestions: string[];
} | const summary = summarize(history);
validateSummary(summary);
const plan = await decompose(task, summary);
validateDecompositionPlan(plan);
await flagship.execute({ task, summary, plan, instructions }); | const STORE_PATH = '.tmp';
const TEMP_OVERWRITE = '.tmp.tmp';
// atomic save: write STORE_PATH + '.tmp' -> fsync -> rename to STORE_PATH (via TEMP_OVERWRITE flow)
Invariants: schema version = 1; file path = .tmp; Runtime validator must stay aligned with TypeScript types to avoid drift; successful mutation preserves `version = 1`; file path = .tmp.tmp; preserve `version = 1`

